# Universal Accessibility & Rendering Patch Guide
## Consolidated Fixes for ARIA, HTML, Themes, and Data Protocols

**Version**: 1.0 | **Target**: Existing Company Websites (Open Source or Proprietary)

---

## Executive Summary

This guide consolidates ARIA accessibility corrections with performance fixes for initialization lag. It targets violations found in `chrome://file-manager` diagnostics while providing framework-agnostic solutions applicable to any existing website.

---

## Part 1: ARIA Accessibility Violations & Fixes

### Common Violation Patterns

| Violation | Invalid Usage | Correct Pattern | WCAG Reference |
|-----------|---------------|-----------------|----------------|
| `aria-setsize` on container | `ul[role="tree"]` with `aria-setsize` | Move to `li[role="treeitem"]` | WAI-ARIA APG Tree |
| `aria-activedescendant` on button | `<button aria-activedescendant="...">` | Remove; manage focus in dropdown | WAI-ARIA Button Pattern |
| Missing accessible name | `<list id="file-list">` without label | Add `aria-label="Items in folder"` | WCAG 4.1.2 Name/Role/Value |
| Duplicate ARIA IDs | Multiple elements with same `id` | Ensure uniqueness or use `aria-describedby` | WCAG 4.1.1 Parsing |
| `aria-hidden` on focusable | `<button aria-hidden="true">` | Never hide interactive elements | BOIA Checklist |

### Fix: Tree Navigation

```html
<!-- BEFORE (INVALID) -->
<ul class="tree" role="tree" aria-setsize="10">
  <li>Item 1</li>
  <li>Item 2</li>
</ul>

<!-- AFTER (VALID) -->
<ul class="tree" role="tree" aria-label="File Navigation">
  <li role="treeitem" aria-setsize="10" aria-selected="false">Item 1</li>
  <li role="treeitem" aria-setsize="10" aria-selected="false">Item 2</li>
</ul>
```

### Fix: Action Buttons with Dropdowns

```html
<!-- BEFORE (INVALID) -->
<button id="sort-button" aria-activedescendant="dropdown-item-1">Sort</button>

<!-- AFTER (VALID) -->
<button id="sort-button" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false">
  Sort
</button>
<ul id="sort-menu" role="menu" hidden>
  <li role="menuitem" tabindex="-1">Name</li>
  <li role="menuitem" tabindex="-1">Date</li>
</ul>
```

### Fix: File List Container Labeling

```html
<!-- BEFORE (NO ACCESSIBLE NAME) -->
<list id="file-list">
  <!-- items -->
</list>

<!-- AFTER (WITH LABEL) -->
<list id="file-list" aria-label="Items in current folder">
  <!-- items -->
</list>

<!-- ALTERNATIVE (LABELLEDBY) -->
<label id="folder-heading">Current Folder Contents</label>
<list id="file-list" aria-labelledby="folder-heading">
  <!-- items -->
</list>
```

