## Part 2: Performance & Rendering Fixes

### Layout Thrashing Mitigation

Replace manual measurement toggles with `ResizeObserver` to eliminate forced synchronous reflows.

```javascript
// BEFORE (CAUSES THRASHING)
function updateMetrics_() {
  this.style.overflowY = 'hidden';
  const width = this.clientWidth;
  this.style.overflowY = 'scroll';
  // layout recalc happens here
  const offsetWidth = this.offsetWidth;
  this.style.overflowY = '';
}

// AFTER (ASYNCHRONOUS, NO THRASHING)
const resizeObserver = new ResizeObserver(entries => {
  for (let entry of entries) {
    const { width, height } = entry.contentRect;
    handleResize({ width, height });
  }
});
resizeObserver.observe(this);

// Cache measurements if needed within same frame
let cachedWidth = null;
function updateMetrics_() {
  if (cachedWidth !== null) return cachedWidth;
  cachedWidth = this.offsetWidth;
  return cachedWidth;
}
```

### Main Thread Yielding During Initialization

Break up synchronous UI construction to improve Interaction to Next Paint (INP).

```javascript
// BEFORE (BLOCKS MAIN THREAD ~250ms)
function initializeUi() {
  initEssentialUi_();
  initAdditionalUi_();
  initDialogComponents();
}

// AFTER (YIELDS BETWEEN TASKS)
async function initializeUi() {
  await initEssentialUi_();
  await scheduler.yield(); // Chromium-specific priority hint
  await initAdditionalUi_();
  // Defer non-critical dialog construction
  await new Promise(resolve => requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    initDialogComponents();
    resolve();
  }));
}
```

### Alternative for Non-Chromium Environments

```javascript
// Fallback when scheduler.yield() unavailable
async function yieldToMainThread() {
  return new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 0));
}
```

